WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
When I was little, I would wake up at night terrified by the idea of death.

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:11.880
My father would comfort me with soft pets and kisses, but he would never lie.

3
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:17.600
We all die, Susie, he would say, it's normal to be scared.

4
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.160
He didn't try to invent a buffer between me and reality.

5
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:27.400
It took me a while to understand the power of how he guided me through those nights.

6
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:33.160
What he showed me is that courage is not an absence of fear.

7
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:38.040
Courage is fear-walking.

8
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.060
Neither of us knew that in ten short years he would be gone, and the time for each of

9
00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:47.640
us is all too precious and all too brief.

10
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:56.640
But when our moment comes to face our fragility in that ultimate time, it will ask us, are

11
00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.960
you agile, are you agile?

12
00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:08.720
Let the moment be an unreserved yes, a yes born of a lifelong correspondence with your

13
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:17.560
own heart, and in seeing yourself, because in seeing yourself, you are also able to

14
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.400
see others too.

15
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:29.880
He only sustainable way forward in a fragile, beautiful world, so well-borner, and thank

16
00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:30.880
you.

17
00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:39.880
Thank you.
